WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.004
- My agent, he watched me really
just be a shell of myself.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.798
He said, "Jeremy, this might
be your last game in the NBA.

00:00:06.798 --> 00:00:09.009
Dude, your back is against the wall.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:12.679
And if you're gonna get
knocked out, do it swinging."

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.681
[Intense music]

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.891
[NBA announcer speaking indistinctly]

00:00:16.891 --> 00:00:18.059
- [Announcer:] Pull-up jump shot.

00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:19.644
It’s good. Jeremy Lin!

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:22.605
[Music intensifies]

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:25.316
[Crowd cheering]
- [Public address announcer:] Jeremy Lin!

00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:28.236
[Upbeat music]

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:30.822
- [Lin:] Basically, what happened
was we played in Boston.

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:32.323
We got back around, you know, whatever,

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:34.200
like, 1 a.m., 2 a.m.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.578
I was on Landry Fields’ couch

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:40.457
because my brother and
sister-in-law had friends in town.

00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:43.334
So they were crashing on the
couch, where I normally crash.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:46.546
And so, by the time we get to
Landry's apartment, he's like,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.590
"This is my couch. I
told you it was small."

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.924
And I was like, "Oh, my goodness.

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:52.052
This is smaller than I thought."

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:55.096
And I had my head hanging off one end,

00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:56.264
legs hanging off the other.

00:00:56.264 --> 00:00:58.600
I was curled up, you
know, in a fetal position.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.810
I still couldn't even fit on the couch.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.730
So I wake up the next morning,
terrible night's rest.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:08.109
So immediately go to StuyTown,
grab a fresh set of clothes,

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:10.195
and I stopped by Papaya Dog.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.030
And then I went to MSG.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.406
And that was just my day.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:17.202
And it was just, like, this
feeling of, like, is this the end?

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:20.371
And, you know, I remember
my agent calling me,

00:01:20.371 --> 00:01:21.748
and he was basically saying like,

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:25.126
"Look, this is probably
your last game in the NBA

00:01:25.126 --> 00:01:28.421
if they even give you an
opportunity to be on the floor."

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.716
He said—and he had been walking with me

00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:36.679
through all my overthinking,
my insecurities, my anxiety.

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:39.849
And he watched me really just be a shell

00:01:39.849 --> 00:01:41.392
of myself my whole rookie year.

00:01:41.392 --> 00:01:43.436
And he told me, he said,

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:46.106
"Jeremy, this might be
your last game in the NBA.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:51.111
If it is, you gotta go out
playing Jeremy Lin basketball."

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.613
And that really stuck with me.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.823
And I was like,

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:59.285
"I gotta swing for the fences
tonight and just go for it."

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.162
- [Announcer:] Jeremy Lin.
[Crowd cheering]

00:02:01.162 --> 00:02:02.122
And you hear a pretty big ovation.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:05.125
- Growing up, New York
basketball was not easy to like.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:08.670
- Basketball in New York
City is its lifeblood,

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.714
and the Knicks have been awful.

00:02:11.714 --> 00:02:13.341
- And he brought energy to the Knicks

00:02:13.341 --> 00:02:16.344
like I've never seen before
and haven't seen since.

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:18.138
- [Lin:] Started, I was loose.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.849
And I just feel like that
was really supernatural

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:23.560
cuz I struggled a lot
with pregame anxiety.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.895
But, like, for whatever reason, that day

00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:29.315
when I got subbed in, I was just ready.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.527
[Electronic dance music]

00:02:32.527 --> 00:02:34.445
If I had four points in
the game, I'd be like,

00:02:34.445 --> 00:02:35.280
"Dude, that's a good game."

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.240
But I was like, "Dude, that's a great half.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.576
Like, I'm really happy with this half."

00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:40.994
But then in the second half,

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.495
like, I don't even know what happened.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.329
It just flowed.
[Crowd cheering]

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.707
It just flowed and I just got in the zone.

00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:49.669
- [Announcer:] Magical night for Jeremy Lin.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:53.590
He's the hero from Harvard
on the game of his life.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:56.968
- Immediately, I went
to eat with my parents.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.512
My phone was just going insane.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.639
Like, I had hundreds of messages.

00:03:02.724 --> 00:03:03.850
And then I got home

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.852
and I was with my
brother and sister-in-law

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.020
and I was about to crash on their couch.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.271
They were like, "Dude, what happened?"

00:03:08.271 --> 00:03:09.939
I was like, "I don't know."
And we were just like...

00:03:09.939 --> 00:03:10.773
we were all in shock.

00:03:10.773 --> 00:03:13.693
And then, I pull up ESPN
and I'm on the front page.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.613
And so now, we're all geeking
out and I'm taking photos

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:17.614
and screenshots.

00:03:17.614 --> 00:03:19.490
The coolest thing about it
was I got to celebrate it

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.327
with the people that I was
closest to, who had been with me,

00:03:22.327 --> 00:03:25.288
who had told me not to quit
when I was ready to quit.

00:03:25.288 --> 00:03:26.539
- [Fan:] Garden was absolutely electric.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.875
Every game felt like Game 7.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.210
Knick fans are still excited,

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.796
but not as exciting as it was
during, you know, Linsanity.

00:03:33.796 --> 00:03:35.673
I became a Knick fan at the time.

00:03:35.673 --> 00:03:38.426
- I think he gave us a lift
at a time when we needed it.

00:03:38.426 --> 00:03:41.054
- Linsanity brought a ton of energy

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:42.805
and a little bit of winning,

00:03:42.805 --> 00:03:44.474
which we didn't have at that time.

00:03:45.516 --> 00:03:48.186
[Techno music]

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.397
- I hated it for years.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:54.525
Like, my whole life, I've always wanted

00:03:54.525 --> 00:03:55.985
to just be, like, Jeremy.

00:03:55.985 --> 00:03:58.321
It almost felt like phenomenon

00:03:58.321 --> 00:04:00.531
which I was never really down with.

00:04:00.531 --> 00:04:05.536
But I realized, like, later,
I came to really accept it

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.580
and embrace it now

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.416
because to some people that was that.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.877
That was, like, such a
moment of inspiration.

00:04:12.877 --> 00:04:15.088
- You know, he could've been a king of New York.

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:17.048
And you just get this hope,

00:04:17.048 --> 00:04:21.427
this energy, this love that
this one guy just brought

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.262
to the city.

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:25.306
And then, just like that, it was gone.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.060
- I was always the underdog.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.687
I was always surprising people.

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:32.522
It was always like, “Oh, he’s better than we thought.”

00:04:32.522 --> 00:04:34.524
So I'd never been in a position

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:36.943
where I had any expectations.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:41.948
Now, it's like, I almost became,
like, public enemy No. 1

00:04:43.157 --> 00:04:45.076
to the New York fanbase.

00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:47.662
And I think what was really
disheartening about it

00:04:47.662 --> 00:04:51.833
was that the claims and the
things that people were saying

00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:53.251
about me weren't true.

00:04:53.251 --> 00:04:55.253
And I think that's what really hurt me.

00:04:55.253 --> 00:04:57.171
And that's when I kind of realized,

00:04:57.171 --> 00:05:00.216
like, perception is reality.

00:05:00.216 --> 00:05:03.344
And I actually tried to, you know,

00:05:03.344 --> 00:05:05.638
go back and ask the Rockets.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.432
I wanted the Rockets to give me less

00:05:07.432 --> 00:05:08.725
so that New York could match.

00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:10.810
I was trying to do
everything behind the scenes

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.437
so I could stay in New York.

00:05:12.437 --> 00:05:15.398
And a lot of what had
happened and the aftermath

00:05:15.398 --> 00:05:19.319
and the fallout, I actually
still to this day am not aware

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:22.822
of why it happened, how
it happened or whatever.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:26.242
But that fallout was one
of the tougher things

00:05:26.242 --> 00:05:27.952
that I've had to experience.

00:05:27.952 --> 00:05:30.788
And it really bothered me deeply.

00:05:30.788 --> 00:05:32.540
And I felt extremely misunderstood.

00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:36.210
[Soft music]

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.962
- You know, there was just this energy

00:05:37.962 --> 00:05:41.841
that's hard to really
vocalize unless you're

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:45.428
from a city or a town
that has a sports team

00:05:45.428 --> 00:05:46.971
that they just love.

00:05:46.971 --> 00:05:48.973
- [Fan:] To see the Garden actually light up,

00:05:48.973 --> 00:05:50.725
changed my perspective on
basketball a little bit.

00:05:50.725 --> 00:05:52.477
- It’s the Knicks. No matter

00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:53.644
whether they’re good or bad,

00:05:53.644 --> 00:05:55.063
no matter what,

00:05:55.063 --> 00:05:56.773
Knicks fans are Knicks fans. They’re
always gonna appreciate that

00:05:56.773 --> 00:05:57.607
no matter what.

00:05:57.607 --> 00:05:58.858
- As a New Yorker,

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.152
I'm glad that we had
Jeremy Lin in our city.

00:06:01.152 --> 00:06:03.321
- Yo, Jeremy, man, we loved you.

00:06:03.321 --> 00:06:04.405
We still love you.

00:06:04.405 --> 00:06:08.034
And I still have all the wristbands,

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:10.286
the Linsanity wristbands, I have about 30

00:06:10.286 --> 00:06:12.955
of ‘em sitting in a box in my house

00:06:12.955 --> 00:06:14.707
and we always—

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.125
- Ah, that's cool.

00:06:18.169 --> 00:06:21.339
Man, I'll always have love for New York.

00:06:21.339 --> 00:06:25.259
Every time I go back, it's just, it’s love.

00:06:25.259 --> 00:06:27.804
Even nine, 10 years later, doesn't matter.

00:06:27.804 --> 00:06:30.515
If I'm back there, it's
like, dude, let me tell you

00:06:30.515 --> 00:06:32.225
where I was when this happened.

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:34.477
Dude, let me tell you
how this impacted me.

00:06:34.477 --> 00:06:37.855
We were thinking about
what's the best way to honor

00:06:37.855 --> 00:06:39.774
the 10-year anniversary of Linsanity.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.070
And we felt like the best
way to honor is to give back

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.572
because the city and the
fans gave us so much.

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:50.827
And so, we're starting
a fundraising campaign

00:06:50.827 --> 00:06:55.665
to be able to give the
profits and the proceeds

00:06:55.665 --> 00:07:00.336
to organizations in New York
to be able to try to help.

00:07:00.336 --> 00:07:03.548
You're looking at setbacks in
education and in resources,

00:07:03.548 --> 00:07:04.632
opportunities.

00:07:04.632 --> 00:07:06.551
You're looking at mental
health issues for youth.

00:07:06.551 --> 00:07:10.388
You're looking at a lot
of delay and restriction

00:07:10.388 --> 00:07:13.015
of access to sports and extracurriculars.

00:07:13.015 --> 00:07:14.642
Like, we're in this together.

00:07:14.642 --> 00:07:16.394
We're a community. We're a humanity.

00:07:16.394 --> 00:07:19.021
And that's what's so
special about this story.

00:07:19.021 --> 00:07:20.231
It could have happened in any city,

00:07:20.231 --> 00:07:24.485
but the fact that it
happened in New York at MSG,

00:07:24.485 --> 00:07:27.488
there's no better city for
it to happen in the world.

